<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anzac Day</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">25 April</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anzac Day, 25 April, is the national day of remembrance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, marking the anniversary of the landing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australian-and-new-zealand-army-corps">Australian and New Zealand Army Corps</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> in 1915. First observed in 1916, it now commemorates all who served and died in military operations, with dawn services, marches and ceremonies in both countries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anzac-day.jpg" alt="Anzac Day" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gnangarra · CC BY 2.5 au · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dawn_service_gnangarra_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
